-- int-tests-chains: whole histories that cross all the headlines, one case file carried through time, each step asked of the integration layer on its own day with the text of the Law of that day.
-- EXPECTED VALUES were decided by hand from the Law before this module was run.  The Order under Article 13(7) and (8) (the due date of the annual return) and the preliminary notice and the notice dates are INPUTS the
-- sources do not supply (no such Order is in the sources): the tests say so and choose illustrative dates.
--
-- CHAIN 1.  Gorey Schools Limited is registered in the general section on 1 March 2019.  An Order makes the annual return for 2019 due on 31 March 2020.
--   1. 2 March 2019: a registered charity in the general section; the seven entries of Article 8(3).  Asked on 28 February 2019 it is not yet entered (G1, G3).
--   2. 1 April 2020: the return was not sent, so the duty of Article 13(7) is breached (G5); that is a contravention of a provision of the Law (IP13), which is misconduct (Article 2(10)(a)(i), G1); the Commissioner may believe it (Article 27(1)(a), G8).
--   3. 10 May 2020: the Commissioner's required steps notice (sent 8 May) is received; its date of service is the date of receipt (Article 38, F7.7); the time is 30 days, so the steps are due by 9 June 2020.
--   4. 15 July 2020: the notice has not been complied with; a preliminary notice of 15 June invited objections to 1 July; the Commissioner may deregister under Article 16(1)(c); the deregistration notice received on 15 July
--      is the date of the deregistration; the information must be retained to 15 July 2030 (Article 17(1)(a)).
--   5. 16 July 2020: the entity is in the historic section and no longer a registered charity (trap T7); the Article 8(5) entries are owed.
--   6. 1 August 2020: the former charity still calls itself a charity: Article 21(1), a strict offence, level 3; its director who connived is also guilty (Article 37(1)).
-- CHAIN 2.  A conviction under this Law is a reportable matter (Article 19(1)(f)): the conviction of step 6 of chain 1, made by headline (d), is carried into headline (c).
-- CHAIN 3.  An NPO body corporate registered on 1 December 2025 under the text with sub-paragraph (ba).

§ `Integration layer -- chains`

GIVETH A `Readings of the fleet`
fleet MEANS `Int the favoured readings of the fleet`

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
      expected IS A LIST OF a
      actual IS A LIST OF a
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the same items` expected actual MEANS
        count expected EQUALS count actual
    AND all (GIVEN x YIELD elem x actual) expected

§§ `Chain 1, step 1: 2 March 2019, a registered charity`

#ASSERT (`Int (b) is the entity a registered charity and what does the register hold` fleet (YMD 2019 3 2) `Int fx the register entry of the school company`)'s `the entity is a registered charity`
#ASSERT (`Int (b) is the entity a registered charity and what does the register hold` fleet (YMD 2019 3 2) `Int fx the register entry of the school company`)'s `section the entity is entered in` EQUALS JUST `the general section`
#ASSERT `the same items` (LIST `a note of the status of the entity`, `the names of each of the governors`, `the principal address`, `the registered charitable purposes`, `the registered public benefit statement`, `the date on which the charity was registered`, `whether the charity has or has not sent its annual return for the most recent year`) ((`Int (b) is the entity a registered charity and what does the register hold` fleet (YMD 2019 3 2) `Int fx the register entry of the school company`)'s `the entries the Commissioner must enter`)
-- The day before the entry (28 February 2019): never yet entered, and the recorded standing does not agree with the entries.
#ASSERT (`Int (b) is the entity a registered charity and what does the register hold` fleet (YMD 2019 2 28) `Int fx the register entry of the school company`)'s `section the entity is entered in` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT NOT (`Int (b) is the entity a registered charity and what does the register hold` fleet (YMD 2019 2 28) `Int fx the register entry of the school company`)'s `the recorded standing agrees with the entries`

§§ `Chain 1, step 2: 1 April 2020, the annual return not sent -- the duty of Article 13(7) is breached (G5), which feeds Article 2(10) (G1) and Article 27 (G8)`

GIVETH AN `Order under Article 13(7) and (8)`
`an Order making the return for 2019 due on 31 March 2020` MEANS
    `Order under Article 13(7) and (8)` WITH `due date of the annual return` IS JUST (YMD 2020 3 31), `consequence of lateness` IS NOTHING
-- Not sent by the due date: the duty is breached on 1 April 2020.
-- EXPECT: BREACH Article 13(7)
#TRACE `Art 13(7) the registered charity must send an annual return` ((fleet)'s `reading of Articles 13 and 14`) TRUE `an Order making the return for 2019 due on 31 March 2020` AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2020 1 1)) WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2020 4 1)))
-- Sent on the due date: timely on the reading taken of F5.5.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 13(7) the registered charity must send an annual return` ((fleet)'s `reading of Articles 13 and 14`) TRUE `an Order making the return for 2019 due on 31 March 2020` AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2020 1 1)) WITH
    PARTY `a registered charity` DOES `send the annual return to the Commissioner` AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2020 3 31))

-- The trace's BREACH is the contravention that the integration layer passes to headline (c).
GIVETH A `Contravention of this Law in the case`
`the annual return was not sent` MEANS
    `a duty or prohibition was breached, as a trace of the rule shows` WITH rule IS "Article 13(7)"

GIVETH A `Contravention case`
`the base case for the chains` MEANS
    `Contravention case` WITH
        charity IS `Int fx the register entry of the school company`
        contraventions IS EMPTY
        conduct IS `Int fx conduct that contravenes nothing`
        `facts for the excepted foreign charity test` IS `Int fx the facts of a Jersey body for Article 22`
        `conduct of the governors` IS LIST (`Int fx a governor whose conduct is clear called` "A. Le Brun")
        `the Commissioner's beliefs` IS EMPTY
        `a governor is unfit by reason of a reportable matter` IS FALSE
        `facts about the grounds of Article 16(1)` IS `Int fx proportionate to deregister`
        `preliminary notice` IS NOTHING
        deregistration IS NOTHING
        `application to the court` IS `an application by the Commissioner`
        `what appears to the court` IS `What appears to the court under Article 14(1)` WITH `the conduct concerns the administration of the charity` IS FALSE, `the conduct is misconduct in the ordinary sense` IS FALSE, `it is necessary or desirable to exercise the power to protect the charity's property or secure its proper application` IS FALSE
        `the charity carries out, or intends to carry out, an activity in or from within Jersey` IS TRUE
        `the activity is, in the opinion of the Commissioner, substantial` IS TRUE
        `a relevant person has been designated under sub-paragraph (4)` IS FALSE
        `the person appointed as the Commissioner is unable to act` IS FALSE
        `there is a vacancy in the office of Commissioner` IS FALSE

GIVETH A `Contravention case`
`the case of the charity that did not send its return` MEANS
    `Int fx the contravention case with the Commissioner's beliefs replaced` (`Int fx the contravention case with conduct replaced` (`Int fx the contravention case with contraventions replaced` `the base case for the chains` (LIST `the annual return was not sent`)) `Int fx conduct by a registered charity or its governor`) (LIST `there has been misconduct by a registered charity`)

#ASSERT (`Int (c) what follows from the contravention` fleet (YMD 2020 4 1) `the case of the charity that did not send its return`)'s `a provision of this Law has been contravened`
#ASSERT (`Int (c) what follows from the contravention` fleet (YMD 2020 4 1) `the case of the charity that did not send its return`)'s `the charity's conduct is misconduct within Article 2(10)`
#ASSERT (`Int (c) what follows from the contravention` fleet (YMD 2020 4 1) `the case of the charity that did not send its return`)'s `the grounds on which the Commissioner may serve a required steps notice` EQUALS LIST `there has been misconduct by a registered charity`
-- The charity's conduct is misconduct, but no governor contravened anything personally: no governor engages in misconduct (Article 18(4)).
#ASSERT (`Int (c) what follows from the contravention` fleet (YMD 2020 4 1) `the case of the charity that did not send its return`)'s `the governors who engage in misconduct within Article 18(4)` EQUALS EMPTY
-- Without the breach, the same charity in the same case has contravened nothing.
#ASSERT NOT (`Int (c) what follows from the contravention` fleet (YMD 2020 4 1) `the base case for the chains`)'s `a provision of this Law has been contravened`

§§ `Chain 1, step 3: 10 May 2020, the required steps notice is served -- the date of service (Article 38, F7.7) and the end of the time it names`

GIVETH A `Notice served in the case`
`the required steps notice of 8 May 2020 received on 10 May 2020` MEANS
    `Notice served in the case` WITH recipient IS `the registered charity`, belief IS `there has been misconduct by a registered charity`, `date sent` IS YMD 2020 5 8, `date received` IS JUST (YMD 2020 5 10), `date fixed by an Order under Article 38` IS NOTHING, time IS `a period of days fixed by the notice` 30, requirements IS EMPTY, `the steps required have been taken` IS FALSE
-- Reading taken of F7.7: the date of service is the date of receipt, 10 May 2020; 30 days after it (the day of service is not counted) is 9 June 2020 (May has 31 days: 10 May + 21 = 31 May, + 9 = 9 June).
#ASSERT `Int IP34 the date on which the notice was served` fleet `the required steps notice of 8 May 2020 received on 10 May 2020` EQUALS YMD 2020 5 10
#ASSERT (`Int IP19 the required steps notice` fleet `the required steps notice of 8 May 2020 received on 10 May 2020`)'s `date served` EQUALS YMD 2020 5 10
#ASSERT (`Int IP19 the required steps notice` fleet `the required steps notice of 8 May 2020 received on 10 May 2020`)'s `steps to be taken by` EQUALS JUST (YMD 2020 6 9)
-- The other reading of F7.7 (the date of service is the date of sending, 8 May 2020): 30 days after it is 7 June 2020 (8 May + 23 = 31 May, + 7 = 7 June).  The fork is one value for the whole fleet; the same notice is served two days earlier.
GIVETH A `Readings of the fleet`
`the readings with F7.7 read as the date of sending` MEANS `Int fx the readings with the reading of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes` fleet `the interpretation with the other reading of F7.7`
#ASSERT `Int IP34 the date on which the notice was served` `the readings with F7.7 read as the date of sending` `the required steps notice of 8 May 2020 received on 10 May 2020` EQUALS YMD 2020 5 8
#ASSERT (`Int IP19 the required steps notice` `the readings with F7.7 read as the date of sending` `the required steps notice of 8 May 2020 received on 10 May 2020`)'s `steps to be taken by` EQUALS JUST (YMD 2020 6 7)
-- The register must then note the notice and the date it was served (Article 8(3)(k)).
GIVETH A `Register entry in the case`
`the school company's register entry with the notice` MEANS
    `Int fx the register entry with notices served replaced` `Int fx the register entry of the school company` (LIST `the required steps notice of 8 May 2020 received on 10 May 2020`)
#ASSERT elem `a note of a required steps notice and of the date on which it was served` ((`Int (b) is the entity a registered charity and what does the register hold` fleet (YMD 2020 5 11) `the school company's register entry with the notice`)'s `the entries the Commissioner must enter`)

§§ `Chain 1, step 4: 15 July 2020, the Commissioner may deregister (Article 16(1)(c)); the effects (Article 17)`

GIVETH A `Preliminary notice of Article 16(1)`
`the preliminary notice of 15 June 2020` MEANS
    `Preliminary notice of Article 16(1)` WITH `given on` IS YMD 2020 6 15, `the last day for objections` IS YMD 2020 7 1, `in writing` IS TRUE, `specifies reasons` IS TRUE, `invites objections within a time it specifies` IS TRUE, `the time specified is reasonable` IS TRUE
GIVETH A `Deregistration of the entity`
`the deregistration of 15 July 2020 for failing to comply with the notice` MEANS
    `Deregistration of the entity` WITH
        route IS `by written notice under Article 16(1) on the ground that the entity has failed to comply with a required steps notice`
        `date of the deregistration` IS YMD 1999 1 1
        `date of the preliminary notice` IS JUST (YMD 2020 6 15)
        `the Commissioner is satisfied that the grounds have existed since` IS NOTHING
        `past date specified in the deregistration notice` IS NOTHING
        `past date specified in the preliminary notice` IS NOTHING
        `the Commissioner determines that the deregistration takes effect retrospectively` IS FALSE
-- The placeholder date 1 January 1999 is replaced by the date of service of the deregistration notice, 15 July 2020 (received that day).
GIVETH A `Deregistration in the case`
`the deregistration in the case, notice received on 15 July 2020` MEANS
    `Deregistration in the case` WITH deregistration IS `the deregistration of 15 July 2020 for failing to comply with the notice`, notice IS `Notice of a decision in the case` WITH `date sent` IS YMD 2020 7 13, `date received` IS JUST (YMD 2020 7 15), `date fixed by an Order under Article 38` IS NOTHING

GIVETH A `Contravention case`
`the case of the charity that failed to comply with the notice` MEANS
    `Int fx the contravention case with deregistration replaced` (`Int fx the contravention case with preliminary notice replaced` (`Int fx the contravention case with charity replaced` `the base case for the chains` `the school company's register entry with the notice`) (JUST `the preliminary notice of 15 June 2020`)) (JUST `the deregistration in the case, notice received on 15 July 2020`)

-- Ground (c) only: the charity meets the charity test, and the time the notice names ran out on 9 June 2020.
#ASSERT (`Int (c) what follows from the contravention` fleet (YMD 2020 7 15) `the case of the charity that failed to comply with the notice`)'s `a ground of Article 16(1) for deregistration exists`
#ASSERT (`Int (c) what follows from the contravention` fleet (YMD 2020 7 15) `the case of the charity that failed to comply with the notice`)'s `the entity meets the charity test`
-- Asked on 1 June 2020, before the time ran out, the charity has not yet failed to comply: no ground.
#ASSERT NOT (`Int (c) what follows from the contravention` fleet (YMD 2020 6 1) `the case of the charity that failed to comply with the notice`)'s `a ground of Article 16(1) for deregistration exists`
-- The power to deregister is open from 2 July 2020 (the preliminary notice's objections ended 1 July) and is not open on 25 June.
-- EXPECT: STANDING MAY
#TRACE `Int (c) the Commissioner may deregister the entity` fleet (YMD 2020 7 15) `the case of the charity that failed to comply with the notice` AT 0 WITH
    -- no events
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Int (c) the Commissioner may deregister the entity` fleet (YMD 2020 7 15) `the case of the charity that failed to comply with the notice` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `deregister the entity by written notice` `the Commissioner` AT 3
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Int (c) the Commissioner may deregister the entity` fleet (YMD 2020 6 25) `the case of the charity that failed to comply with the notice` AT 0 WITH
    -- no events
-- Article 17: the basis is the failure to comply with the notice; not retrospective; the date deregistered is the date of service of the deregistration notice, 15 July 2020; the information must be retained
-- for 10 years, to the anniversary 15 July 2030 (F6.5, F6.18 on the readings taken).
#ASSERT (`Int (c) what follows from the contravention` fleet (YMD 2020 7 15) `the case of the charity that failed to comply with the notice`)'s `the effects of the deregistration` EQUALS JUST (`Effects of a deregistration` WITH `the basis of the deregistration` IS `the entity has failed to comply with a required steps notice`, `date deregistered` IS YMD 2020 7 15, `the deregistration takes effect retrospectively` IS FALSE, `last day on which the Commissioner must retain the information` IS YMD 2030 7 15)

