§§ `Chain 1, step 6: 1 August 2020, the former charity still calls itself a charity -- Article 21(1), priced -- and its director who connived is also guilty (Article 37(1))`

GIVETH AN `Act alleged in the case`
`the former charity calls itself a charity` MEANS
    `a statement about an entity` WITH
        body IS `the deregistered school company`
        `facts for the excepted foreign charity test` IS `Int fx the facts of a Jersey body for Article 22`
        `the entity is wholly or mainly managed or controlled in or from within Jersey` IS TRUE
        statement IS `Int fx a statement by the entity itself saying` `that it is a “charity”`
GIVETH AN `Offence case`
`the offence case of the former charity and its director` MEANS
    `Offence case` WITH act IS `the former charity calls itself a charity`, officer IS JUST (`Int fx an officer who connived, of` `a body corporate` `a director of the body corporate`)
GIVETH A `Penalty provided`
`level 3 and no imprisonment` MEANS
    `Penalty provided` WITH `imprisonment up to, in months` IS NOTHING, fine IS `a fine of a level on the standard scale` 3
-- A formerly registered entity is not a registered charity (trap T7): the statement contravenes 21(1), a strict offence at level 3 (21(10)); the director who connived is guilty too (37(1)), with the same penalty.
#ASSERT (`Int (d) the offence and the penalty for the act` fleet (YMD 2020 8 1) `the offence case of the former charity and its director`)'s `an offence is made out`
#ASSERT (`Int (d) the offence and the penalty for the act` fleet (YMD 2020 8 1) `the offence case of the former charity and its director`)'s penalties EQUALS LIST `level 3 and no imprisonment`
#ASSERT (`Int (d) the offence and the penalty for the act` fleet (YMD 2020 8 1) `the offence case of the former charity and its director`)'s `the officer is also guilty under Article 37(1)`
#ASSERT (`Int (d) the offence and the penalty for the act` fleet (YMD 2020 8 1) `the offence case of the former charity and its director`)'s `the penalties of the officer` EQUALS LIST `level 3 and no imprisonment`
-- Before the deregistration the same words, said by the registered charity, are no offence.
GIVETH AN `Act alleged in the case`
`the registered charity calls itself a charity` MEANS
    `a statement about an entity` WITH
        body IS `Int fx the registered school company`
        `facts for the excepted foreign charity test` IS `Int fx the facts of a Jersey body for Article 22`
        `the entity is wholly or mainly managed or controlled in or from within Jersey` IS TRUE
        statement IS `Int fx a statement by the entity itself saying` `that it is a “charity”`
#ASSERT NOT (`Int (d) the offence and the penalty for the act` fleet (YMD 2020 7 1) (`Offence case` WITH act IS `the registered charity calls itself a charity`, officer IS NOTHING))'s `an offence is made out`

§§ `Chain 2: the conviction of chain 1, step 6, is a reportable matter -- a result of headline (d) carried into headline (c)`

-- The director is convicted of the offence that headline (d) found made out (an offence under this Law); the conviction is not spent; any conviction, spent or not, for an offence under this Law is a reportable matter
-- (Article 19(1)(f)).  The conviction record is built from headline (d)'s own answer, so that if (d) found no offence the conviction would not be "for an offence under this Law".
GIVETH A `Facts about a person for Article 19(1)`
`the facts of a governor convicted of the offence found by headline (d)` MEANS
    `Facts about a person for Article 19(1)` WITH
        `conduct as a governor` IS `Int fx the clear conduct of` "A. Le Brun"
        `the governors of the charity` IS EMPTY
        `the conduct of the charity is misconduct within Article 2(10)` IS FALSE
        `the misconduct led to the service of a required steps notice` IS FALSE
        `disqualification orders under this Law` IS EMPTY
        `subject to another restriction on acting as a governor under this Law` IS FALSE
        `disqualifications as a charity trustee or an equivalent` IS EMPTY
        `disqualifications as a company director or an equivalent outside Jersey` IS EMPTY
        `bankrupt or otherwise insolvent` IS FALSE
        convictions IS LIST (`Conviction of a person` WITH `for an offence under this Law` IS (`Int (d) the offence and the penalty for the act` fleet (YMD 2020 8 1) `the offence case of the former charity and its director`)'s `the officer is also guilty under Article 37(1)`, `for an offence falling within Article 2(10)(b)` IS FALSE, spent IS FALSE)
        `falls within another description prescribed by Order` IS FALSE
GIVETH A `Person in the case`
`the convicted director` MEANS
    `Person in the case` WITH
        considered IS (`Int fx a director with nothing to report called` "A. Le Brun")'s considered
        `facts for the reportable matters` IS `the facts of a governor convicted of the offence found by headline (d)`
        `made a report under paragraph (2)` IS FALSE
        `provided a declaration of no reportable matter` IS FALSE
        `reported matter awaiting determination` IS NOTHING
GIVETH A `Register entry in the case`
`the register entry of a school company with a convicted director` MEANS
    `Int fx the register entry with body replaced` `Int fx the register entry of the school company` (`Body in the case` WITH name IS "Gorey Schools Limited", standing IS `entered in the general section`, purposes IS ((`Int fx the registered school company`)'s purposes), facts IS ((`Int fx the registered school company`)'s facts), model IS `Int fx clear model facts`, people IS LIST `the convicted director`)
GIVETH A `Contravention case`
`the case of a school company with a convicted director` MEANS
    `Int fx the contravention case with charity replaced` `the base case for the chains` `the register entry of a school company with a convicted director`
#ASSERT (`Int (c) what follows from the contravention` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) `the case of a school company with a convicted director`)'s `the reportable matters of each governor` EQUALS LIST (`Reportable matters of a governor` OF "A. Le Brun", (LIST `a conviction, whether or not spent, for an offence under this Law`))

